# W Linux — re-evaluates the night light once a minute.
#
# A minute is the right granularity for the one job this has left: noticing that
# the goal and the screen have parted company — a window boundary just passed, a
# suspend ended, the daemon crashed and came back neutral — and handing the job
# to w-nightlight-ramp.service, which owns the transition itself and steps it far
# faster than any timer would.
#
# ⚠️ This timer is NOT the ramp mechanism, and trying to make it one is a dead
# end that was tried: the target used to be computed in whole MINUTES, so a
# sub-minute tick recomputed an identical value and skipped it, and no tick rate
# could make a transition any smoother. The goal is second-resolution now and the
# stepping lives in the ramp unit.
#
# AccuracySec lets systemd coalesce this with other timers instead of waking the
# machine on its own schedule — the work is a comparison that almost always ends
# in "nothing to do", and it is not worth a dedicated wakeup.
#
# WantedBy=graphical-session.target (not timers.target): the night light is a
# property of a running desktop session, and it must stop with it. See
# w-nightlight.md.
#
# ⚠️ `After=graphical-session.target` is load-bearing, not tidiness. Without it
# this timer is condition-checked WHILE the target is coming up — about a second
# before uwsm exports WAYLAND_DISPLAY into the user manager — so
# ConditionEnvironment fails, systemd logs one "skipped, unmet condition" line
# and the timer never starts for the WHOLE session. The schedule then only ever
# moved when something called a setter (the Hub, the hotkey, apply.sh), which is
# exactly what "the night light works some days and not others" looked like from
# the outside. Measured on hardware 2026-08-07: timer condition-checked at
# 16:52:00.47, WAYLAND_DISPLAY exported at 16:52:01.47, target reached at
# 16:52:02.35. The packaged hyprsunset.service and hypridle.service never fell
# into this because upstream orders them After= the target — copy that, always,
# for anything wanted by a target whose environment arrives together with it.
[Unit]
Description=W night light — periodic schedule evaluation
After=graphical-session.target
PartOf=graphical-session.target
ConditionEnvironment=WAYLAND_DISPLAY

[Timer]
OnStartupSec=30s
OnUnitActiveSec=60s
AccuracySec=20s
Unit=w-nightlight-tick.service

[Install]
WantedBy=graphical-session.target
